20oz|n|A coarse blackish seaweed (Fuscus nodosus). ; A strong or offensive taste; especially, a taste of something extraneous to the thing itself; as, wine or cider has a tang of the cask. ; Fig.: A sharp, specific flavor or tinge. Cf. Tang a twang. ; A projecting part of an object by means of which it is secured to a handle, or to some other part; anything resembling a tongue in form or position. ; The part of a knife, fork, file, or other small instrument, which is inserted into the handle. ; The projecting part of the breech of a musket barrel, by which the barrel is secured to the stock. ; The part of a sword blade to which the handle is fastened. ; The tongue of a buckle. ; A sharp, twanging sound; an unpleasant tone; a twang.	n:hqf,116,5~hqf,116,5	N:mq1,148,1;1tsz,42,3~1tsz,42,3;mq1,148,1
