20qu|n|A gentle or slight blow; a light rap; a pat. ; A piece of leather fastened upon the bottom of a boot or shoe in repairing or renewing the sole or heel. ; A signal, by drum or trumpet, for extinguishing all lights in soldiers' quarters and retiring to bed, -- usually given about a quarter of an hour after tattoo. ; A hole or pipe through which liquor is drawn. ; A plug or spile for stopping a hole pierced in a cask, or the like; a faucet. ; Liquor drawn through a tap; hence, a certain kind or quality of liquor; as, a liquor of the same tap. ; A place where liquor is drawn for drinking; a taproom; a bar. ; A tool for forming an internal screw, as in a nut, consisting of a hardened steel male screw grooved longitudinally so as to have cutting edges.	a:rtm,74,4;2f8,69,4;ujc,38,5;1wry,37,3;wn4,31,2;lzo,24,43;t46,22,4;1u2r,21,4;23ta,17,3;1v0y,13,3;248w,8,1;20qu,7,6;1uus,0,22~lzo,24,43;1uus,0,22;20qu,7,6;ujc,38,5;2f8,69,4;1u2r,21,4;t46,22,4;rtm,74,4;1wry,37,3;23ta,17,3;1v0y,13,3;wn4,31,2;248w,8,1	v:rtm,64,2;8qs,51,2;mb0,51,2~8qs,51,2;rtm,64,2;mb0,51,2	V:m4u,13,2;1mxj,12,4;swd,10,3;ikh,9,1;27xl,6,5~27xl,6,5;1mxj,12,4;swd,10,3;m4u,13,2;ikh,9,1	n:bz0,46,4;mb0,41,1;wn4,37,3;rtl,28,15;tz7,27,3;23ta,25,5;225x,15,4;1pdi,8,1;95i,7,5;hsn,6,4~rtl,28,15;23ta,25,5;95i,7,5;hsn,6,4;bz0,46,4;225x,15,4;wn4,37,3;tz7,27,3;mb0,41,1;1pdi,8,1	N:hpa,36,3;uoq,22,3;1ui1,21,1;mpg,18,3;278n,16,2;29bl,14,2;hn,9,2;ikh,9,1;1fq8,8,4;22df,7,2;2h8,6,2;25n9,5,3;1u8j,5,2;m4u,3,1;d3n,3,1~epf,1,4;1fq8,8,4;uoq,22,3;hpa,36,3;25n9,5,3;mpg,18,3;hn,9,2;22df,7,2;1u8j,5,2;2h8,6,2;278n,16,2;29bl,14,2;ikh,9,1;m4u,3,1;1ui1,21,1
